## SQ-SALT2-19 | generated Rock Salt Blocks are never licks; any later placement (/setblock included) is one
@phase worldgen
@group B
@commands Group B seed: `locate biome minecraft:beach`, forceload the 65x65 block area around it (chunks generate with the world), count `hearthandharvest:placed_rock_salt_block` (must be 0) and `salt:raw_rock_salt_block` (recorded); then above the beach at y 150: `/setblock salt:raw_rock_salt_block`, a `/fill` of 3, a piston pushing one placed block one step
@pass no placed twin in untouched generated terrain; the `/setblock` and `/fill` blocks read `hearthandharvest:placed_rock_salt_block`; the pushed block is still `placed_rock_salt_block` one step on (a piston push is not a placement; a pushed generated block is not reachable by command, only by worldgen)
@fails generated blocks already twins: the swap hooks a path world generation takes (`BlockPlaceLickMixin` on the wrong method); /setblock block not a lick: mixin not applied (latest.log mixin errors, SRG `m_6807_`); pushed block lost: moving-piston check in `SaltEvents.afterPlace`
@reviewed 2026-11-26
